  "summary": {
   "status": "complete",
   "text": "James Wolff said cybersecurity cannot be handled by humans alone and requires smart machines. In a 2023 statement, he described a world where sensors far outnumber management capacity, calling it a data science problem. He said early experimentation showed AI was at least additive and potentially disruptive, and that it makes work better and faster.",
